  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Cyclone Akvan impacted India’s east coast, prompting large-scale evacuations of approximately 300,000 residents across Odisha and Andhra Pradesh. As the system made landfall and subsequently weakened into a depression, it caused significant rainfall in low-lying areas, particularly impacting the Ichchapuram and Sompeta regions of Srikakulam. The India Meteorological Department (IMD) has issued ongoing weather warnings, noting that the remnants of the storm are expected to produce thunderstorms and gusty winds in both south and north Bengal through November 22. Regional infrastructure faced challenges, including train cancellations and the adjournment of the Odisha Assembly. Currently, local authorities are focused on flood mitigation, including the controlled release of water from reservoirs, while weather forecasts indicate a transition toward the resumption of monsoon conditions in parts of Tamil Nadu.",
